Attached is a minor update of the SENFS requirements document, following 
initial feedback from the lists.

I'm leaving this document as SELinux-specific, as we need to capture the 
specific SELinux requirements regardless of whether a generic Labeled NFS 
scheme is implemented.  This is the main area that we need further 
feedback on at this stage.


Also at:
http://namei.org/selinux/nfs/senfs-requirements-draft-06.txt

Changes:
- Removed "External Remote Filesystems", which was based on a 
  misinterpretation of the NFSv4.1 draft.
- Added consideration of Labeled NFS as a generic security labeling layer 
  upon which SENFS might be implemented.
- Added more detail to "3.14 Namespace Access", re. MLS polyinstantiation



-- 
James Morris
